  "configuration_id": "config_016",
  "reason": "We have only one completed experiment (config_001: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000, acc≈0.485), so evidence is extremely sparse. The most fundamental question for a multimodal cellular profiling study is whether adding the image modality provides any signal beyond the RNA baseline. Config_016 (multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, concat) is the cleanest logical extension of config_001: it keeps the RNA encoder (pca_n2000) and profile setting (singleprofile) identical, and introduces only the image modality with the simplest reasonable choices (resnet50, concat fusion). This isolates the effect of adding image information. If config_016 substantially exceeds 0.485, it confirms image is a useful modality and justifies further investment in image encoder and fusion choices. If it does not, it tells us the image signal is weak or poorly captured by resnet50, redirecting budget toward RNA encoder or profile-setting improvements. Under a limited budget, answering 'does the second modality help at all?' before exploring encoder variants, multiprofile aggregation, or fusion strategies is the highest-information next step."
}

